    "chunk_text": "III fldgi \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2025'08'15PART III \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 15.08.2025\n\n1A\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n1A \u2013 G 045147 \u201314 (08/2025)\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nOrder under Section 39(a) (1)\n\nTHE allotments specified as the Lot A to DL in the Order No.54 of 2019 made under Proviso (a) to Section 38 of the Land Acquisition Act, (Chapter 460) and published in the Gazette Extraordinary No. 2115/47 dated 22nd March 2019 of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka are vested absolutely in the State and the possession of which has been taken for or on behalf of the State under Paragraph (a) of Section 40 of the aforesaid Act. But by the virtue of Powers vested in me by Sub section (1) of Section 39 (a) (inserted by Act, No. 8 of 1979) of the Land Acquisition Act, I, Kuragamage Don Lal Kantha, Minister of Agriculture Livestock, Land and Irrigation, do hereby divest only the allotments specified in the Schedule I below.\n\nK. D. Lal Kantha, Minister of Agriculture, Livestock, Land and Irrigation.\n\nMy Ref. No.: LD/05/2010/MV/93AII \u0dc0\u0dd9\u0dd9\u0dc5\u0dd4\u0db8. Land Acquiring Officer\u2019s No.: 11/3/3/1/24/C.Ministry of Agriculture Livestock, Land and Irrigation,\u201cMihikatha Medura\u201d, Land secretariat, 1200/6, Rajamalwatta Road, Battaramulla.24th July, 2025.\n\nSCHEDULE I\n\nThe allotments of land in the revised Topographical Preliminary Plan No.20, Inset No.181, Sheet No.247 dated 03.02.2020 prepared by the Surveyor General, situated in the village called Kaluganga in No. E402F, Kaluganga Grama Niladhari Division in the Divisional Secretary's Division of Laggala in Matale District of Central Province and bounded as follows:\n\n01. Lot No.9140 \u2013 Kaluganga \u2013 Extent: 0.0350 Hectare North: Lot Nos.8920,8919,8915 and 9155; East: Lot No.9155; South: Lot Nos.9155,9141 and 9027; West: Lot Nos.9026 and 8920."
